# AddPathNoise.srv
#
# Server: amiga_ros2_planners' path_noise_node. Sits between the planner
# (move_to_node's own control_points -> nav_msgs/Path sampling) and Nav2's
# FollowPath: move_to_node calls this once per walk, right after building
# its nominal Path and before sending the FollowPath goal, and sends the
# RETURNED path to FollowPath instead of the nominal one. Gated by
# move_to_node's own enable_path_noise parameter -- when false, the call
# is skipped entirely (byte-for-byte the behavior before this node
# existed), not just left to this service's own zero-sigma pass-through.
#
# Implements the "deterministic executor, noisy reference" approach: Nav2
# stays a plain, deterministic path follower; the probabilistic motion
# model lives here instead, generating ONE open-loop noisy realization of
# the nominal path offline, which FollowPath then tracks faithfully. With
# both sigmas 0 (or the position.lateral/tangential config.yaml section
# missing entirely), the realization equals nominal_path exactly byte-for-
# byte -- see path_noise.py's own add_path_noise() docstring for the exact
# noise model.
#
# nominal_speed_mps/step_dt_s (ds = nominal_speed_mps * step_dt_s) are
# path_noise_node's OWN parameters, not part of this request:
# problog_project's own config.yaml motion.speed and Nav2's own
# controller_server.controller_frequency respectively -- both per-problem
# constants a caller shouldn't vary walk-to-walk, not something to
# recompute on every call.

# The planner's own nominal path, in whatever frame move_to_node built it
# in (typically "map") -- same convention PlanPath.srv's own response
# documents.
nav_msgs/Path nominal_path

---
# Response

# The noisy open-loop realization, same frame/header as nominal_path,
# resampled at path_noise_node's own fixed arc-length step. Identical to
# nominal_path (not just statistically -- byte-for-byte unchanged) when
# both sigmas are 0.
nav_msgs/Path noisy_path
